{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1546670-seances-ouija-boards-and-paradox","id":1546670,"title":"Seances, Ouija Boards, and Paradox","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-12-05T19:03:53-08:00","id":1546670,"title":"Seances, Ouija Boards, and Paradox","content":"A situation recently came up in game which I'm having trouble finding a good example of in the written material.<br /> <br /> If a mage were to attract the attention of a spirit for purposes of communication, using some form of traditional tool such as a seance or Ouija board, does consensus consider the mage &quot;responsible&quot; if said spirit gets it into mind to perpetrate antics which would be vulgar for the mage to have performed themselves? I'm talking about things which couldn't easily be written off as the tricks of a professional sleeper medium.<br /> <br /> I'm of two minds about this. On one hand, the mage isn't meddling with the tapestry to vulgar effect themselves. On the other, there is the concept of getting burned by a fire you started, given that the spirit wouldn't have been inspired to supernatural tomfoolery otherwise (or at least not this particular instance of tomfoolery.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28664-steve-bridger","name":"Steve Bridger","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-05T19:23:17-08:00","id":1546671,"title":"","content":"No. Spirits don\u2019t use awakened magic and don\u2019t generate Paradox. Also, Paradox is calculated when the spell is cast. Aftereffects and after the fact witnesses generally don\u2019t garner more Paradox.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-05T19:45:16-08:00","id":1546672,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1546670-seances-ouija-boards-and-paradox?p=1546671#post1546671\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No. Spirits don\u2019t use awakened magic and don\u2019t generate Paradox. Also, Paradox is calculated when the spell is cast. Aftereffects and after the fact witnesses generally don\u2019t garner more Paradox.</div> </div> </div> </div>I suppose that's the most logical way of looking at it, and her aunt having a nervous breakdown in the wake of that ordeal is probably enough in the way of consequences. I just had this funny mental image of her pointing to thin air and telling the Hypothetical Average Observer, &quot;It wasn't me, he did it!&quot;<br /> <br /> This sort of thing might be another reason why it's highly unwise to challenge a Dreamspeaker on their own low-gauntlet turf, as they may well have friends who aren't particularly worried about consensus.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28664-steve-bridger","name":"Steve Bridger","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-06T00:40:33-08:00","id":1546679,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1546670-seances-ouija-boards-and-paradox?p=1546671#post1546671\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No. Spirits don\u2019t use awakened magic and don\u2019t generate Paradox. Also, Paradox is calculated when the spell is cast. Aftereffects and after the fact witnesses generally don\u2019t garner more Paradox.</div> </div> </div> </div>While this is true RAW i think it makes more sense to assign paradox per breach. So if someone has a locked ongoing spell on himself allowing him to do telekinesis he in my opinion should get paradox every time he uses it in a vulgar way.<br /> <br /> As for spirits they do not generate paradox thats why fetishes are awesome.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-06T03:45:19-08:00","id":1546681,"title":"","content":"Keep in mind the game has Pattern Bleed and Permanent Paradox for mages that cast long term magic on themselves without being careful about what they're doing. It might not be the same as a backlash every time you use a vulgar effect with a long duration, but it's still some tools for keeping magic in check.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-06T06:24:06-08:00","id":1546686,"title":"","content":"Also Unbelief, which is sometimes called a form of Paradox and sometimes not. It's not mechanically defined, but it is the element that keeps obvious and unbelievable things from sticking around forever.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-06T07:07:58-08:00","id":1546687,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1546670-seances-ouija-boards-and-paradox?p=1546681#post1546681\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Keep in mind the game has Pattern Bleed and Permanent Paradox for mages that cast long term magic on themselves without being careful about what they're doing. It might not be the same as a backlash every time you use a vulgar effect with a long duration, but it's still some tools for keeping magic in check.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah that works only on effects you keep on your self more than a day in case of pattern bleed and permament in case of perm paradox. It can be abused by just putting the effect in the sanctum when you wake up and disabling it before going to sleep.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-06T07:45:02-08:00","id":1546689,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1546670-seances-ouija-boards-and-paradox?p=1546687#post1546687\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah that works only on effects you keep on your self more than a day in case of pattern bleed and permament in case of perm paradox. It can be abused by just putting the effect in the sanctum when you wake up and disabling it before going to sleep.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don\u2019t see the need for a rules patch for this. There are other consequences than points of Paradox for situations like this. Unbelief, notoriety, etc.<br /> <br /> Also, if you really do find a background like Sanctum becoming that powerful, remember that it also makes it a weakness. Sooner or later someone will notice how important that place is to the mage and put it in danger.<br /> <br /> Note that I am not proposing taking the sanctum away, that\u2019s nasty, domineering, and a waste of story potential besides. Instead I suggest putting it in check and making the player respond.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-06T09:26:34-08:00","id":1546692,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1546670-seances-ouija-boards-and-paradox?p=1546689#post1546689\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don\u2019t see the need for a rules patch for this. There are other consequences than points of Paradox for situations like this. Unbelief, notoriety, etc.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>And thats fine. You do what works for you. For me its not enough.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-06T09:51:39-08:00","id":1546693,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1546670-seances-ouija-boards-and-paradox?p=1546692#post1546692\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And thats fine. You do what works for you. For me its not enough.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Fair. The only thing I'd ask, then, is if you've seen this happen or if you only anticipate it happening?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-06T10:10:40-08:00","id":1546694,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1546670-seances-ouija-boards-and-paradox?p=1546693#post1546693\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Fair. The only thing I'd ask, then, is if you've seen this happen or if you only anticipate it happening?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yup i have a party with a very exploit oriented mentality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-06T14:04:36-08:00","id":1546703,"title":"","content":"Given the circumstances under which a Quija board is used Paradox seems wildly unlikely.<br /> <br /> Total skeptics will be expecting a trick or a subconscious reaction where people trick themselves into believing something happened. Any phenomenon will be dismissed as a mere part of the show or simply what happens when we all get silly. Even a levitating planchette or whatever they call it won't be proof of anything except a wild evening.<br /> <br /> It's like using magic to fake a stage magic act. Yes, you are breaking the rules. The universe won't care.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":857,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","user":"Astromancer","date":". 12-06-2024, 05:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-06T19:02:28-08:00","id":1546712,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1546670-seances-ouija-boards-and-paradox?p=1546703#post1546703\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Given the circumstances under which a Quija board is used Paradox seems wildly unlikely.<br /> <br /> Total skeptics will be expecting a trick or a subconscious reaction where people trick themselves into believing something happened. Any phenomenon will be dismissed as a mere part of the show or simply what happens when we all get silly. Even a levitating planchette or whatever they call it won't be proof of anything except a wild evening.<br /> <br /> It's like using magic to fake a stage magic act. Yes, you are breaking the rules. The universe won't care.</div> </div> </div> </div>Under normal circumstances consensus can &quot;overlook&quot; a bit of the supernatural during a seance, or some event where the average observer expects to see something a bit odd but explainable as trickery (even if it's one's own mind likely to be doing the tricking in context.)<br /> <br /> In this particular instance, the mage was asked to help her aunt a bit with a mildly annoying poltergeist, who had previously been reasonably subtle as far as hauntings go. However, the wraith was taken by surprise when confronted by someone with abilities it had not experienced previously and became unhinged (with some inspiration from its shadow.) It then proceeded to unleash a good bit of Pandemonium which went well beyond the pale as suspension of disbelief goes. At that point I was prompted to wonder if consensus might engage in a bit of finger wagging, given that there was an active Spirit effect involved in the whole incident. However, I suppose being forced to deal with the aftermath of it was punishment enough for a bit amateur spiritualism gone very wrong.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28664-steve-bridger","name":"Steve Bridger","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-06T19:18:45-08:00","id":1546713,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1546670-seances-ouija-boards-and-paradox?p=1546689#post1546689\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don\u2019t see the need for a rules patch for this. There are other consequences than points of Paradox for situations like this. Unbelief, notoriety, etc.<br /> <br /> Also, if you really do find a background like Sanctum becoming that powerful, remember that it also makes it a weakness. Sooner or later someone will notice how important that place is to the mage and put it in danger.<br /> <br /> Note that I am not proposing taking the sanctum away, that\u2019s nasty, domineering, and a waste of story potential besides. Instead I suggest putting it in check and making the player respond.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Looking at it from an atmospheric perspective, there's a certain sort of theme in stories about magic which lasts only a certain amount of time (sunset to sunrise, until the rooster crows again, etc.) Mages being smart enough to avoid keeping certain sorts of effects applied to themselves for more than a day sort of fits into that running element, or at least works nicely to explain why those sorts of &quot;limitations&quot; keep cropping up in old tales.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28664-steve-bridger","name":"Steve Bridger","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-09T18:06:53-08:00","id":1546822,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1546670-seances-ouija-boards-and-paradox?p=1546679#post1546679\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> While this is true RAW i think it makes more sense to assign paradox per breach. So if someone has a locked ongoing spell on himself allowing him to do telekinesis he in my opinion should get paradox every time he uses it in a vulgar way.<br /> <br /> As for spirits they do not generate paradox thats why fetishes are awesome.</div> </div> </div> </div>That would be Permadox (permanent Paradox) that follows the Mage until he stops cheating reality.<br /> <br /> You can't dodge Paradox by simply casting permanent effects at the safety of your Sanctum.<br /> <br /> I do however, Houserule that &quot;Permadox&quot; is bled out of you remain within the confines of your sanitized Sanctuary with your private Consensus bubble. So, for instance, if in your Lab &quot;Cyborg-zation&quot; is &quot;coincidental&quot;, then you don't get Permadox (nor Paradox), but step out of your Sanctum, and reality hits you hard with a good dose of Permadox. But that's my own house rule.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-09T18:19:52-08:00","id":1546824,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1546670-seances-ouija-boards-and-paradox?p=1546703#post1546703\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Given the circumstances under which a Quija board is used Paradox seems wildly unlikely.<br /> <br /> Total skeptics will be expecting a trick or a subconscious reaction where people trick themselves into believing something happened. Any phenomenon will be dismissed as a mere part of the show or simply what happens when we all get silly. Even a levitating planchette or whatever they call it won't be proof of anything except a wild evening.<br /> <br /> It's like using magic to fake a stage magic act. Yes, you are breaking the rules. The universe won't care.</div> </div> </div> </div>Quija, Oija... I find so funny the English pronunciation of that... Here in Brazil it is &quot;Orix\u00e1s&quot;, which would probably be unpronounceable for you guys, but that's the name of the entities (Gods?) of their pantheon... My wife believes in that stuff by the way. I don't know what the board in particular is called in here. They refer to it as &quot;white table&quot;, and use it to communicate with the deceased and with other spirits (the Orix\u00e1s, the spiritual guides). <br /> <br /> And yes, I am a skeptical atheist. Fully materialist, fully mechanicist. You won't find a &quot;soul&quot; more adverse to any ideas of the supernatural than me. And I'm married to a women that is a follower of Umbanda which is a Brazilian religion with African origin. Quite a pair. And I've went with her in several of their sessions... And it is quite a show. For me it is a true spectacle. Which I can only describe as self hypnosis episodes - with some more unscrupulous members being outright charlatans. My very own wife gets &quot;possessed&quot; on several of these episodes. Again, self hypnosis.<br /> <br /> Or maybe it is real and spirits exists, who knows, but I wouldn't bet on that.<br /> <br /> Ive also seem similar stuff in Christian congregations thou. I've had a former Christian girlfriend. &quot;Talking in tongues&quot; is not too different from that notion of &quot;the spirit of Eshu (Ex\u00fa in Portuguese) has incorporated on me&quot;. Heck, my wife starts speaking funny during such episodes, but it's not much different from Christians spewing gibberish in their churchs.<br /> <br /> So yes, it doesn't matter what happens in a temple/church/mosque/masonic lodge/sinagogue. Someone like me will just dismiss it as self hypnosis, charlatanism or a magic spectacle. Because that's exactly what I do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-11T22:14:02-08:00","id":1546893,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1546670-seances-ouija-boards-and-paradox?p=1546686#post1546686\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also Unbelief, which is sometimes called a form of Paradox and sometimes not. It's not mechanically defined, but it is the element that keeps obvious and unbelievable things from sticking around forever.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll have to push back against Unbelief not being mechanically defined. See <b>Gods and Monsters</b>, page 199. Granted, that's about how Unbelief affects Bygones, as opposed to how it affects ongoing Effects. Which, from my reading, doesn't happen: with the sole exception of dispelling illusions, which is covered by the &quot;I Disbelieve!&quot; chart on p.504, there doesn't appear to be anything that causes magick to fail under the withering gaze of the skeptic. It can only be subjected to Countermagick. The only blurring of <i>that </i>line appears to be the Negation Men, a type of Marauder introduced in <b>Book of Secrets</b> (pp.248\u2013249) who are in the throes of Denial and weaponize that by instinctively and subconsciously casting Countermagick against any Effects that contradict their world view.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":".  Typo 12-12-2024, 01:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-12T09:33:23-08:00","id":1546903,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1546670-seances-ouija-boards-and-paradox?p=1546893#post1546893\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'll have to push back against Unbelief not being mechanically defined. See <b>Gods and Monsters</b>, page 199. Granted, that's about how Unbelief affects Bygones, as opposed to how it affects ongoing Effects. Which, from my reading, doesn't happen: with the sole exception of dispelling illusions, which is covered by the &quot;I Disbelieve!&quot; chart on p.504, there doesn't appear to be anything that causes magick to fail under the withering gaze of the skeptic. It can only be subjected to Countermagick. The only blurring of <i>that </i>line appears to be the Negation Men, a type of Marauder introduced in <b>Book of Secrets</b> (pp.248\u2013249) who are in the throes of Denial and weaponize that by instinctively and subconsciously casting Countermagick against any Effects that contradict their world view.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair about rules for Unbelief affecting bygones, though it still stands that the way it plays with long term effects is undefined. And from the way it is described in M20, it should be interacting with awakened magic in some way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-12T18:44:42-08:00","id":1546910,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1546670-seances-ouija-boards-and-paradox?p=1546893#post1546893\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'll have to push back against Unbelief not being mechanically defined. See <b>Gods and Monsters</b>, page 199. Granted, that's about how Unbelief affects Bygones, as opposed to how it affects ongoing Effects. Which, from my reading, doesn't happen: with the sole exception of dispelling illusions, which is covered by the &quot;I Disbelieve!&quot; chart on p.504, there doesn't appear to be anything that causes magick to fail under the withering gaze of the skeptic. It can only be subjected to Countermagick. The only blurring of <i>that </i>line appears to be the Negation Men, a type of Marauder introduced in <b>Book of Secrets</b> (pp.248\u2013249) who are in the throes of Denial and weaponize that by instinctively and subconsciously casting Countermagick against any Effects that contradict their world view.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have some vague memories of it being mentioned in earlier editions, but again, never in a defined and with game mechanics behind it. It's just &quot;magik can be subject to Unbelief&quot;.<br /> <br /> I think it is one of the things they always wanted to implement but got sidetracked until ultimately forgotten in M20.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-13T00:25:02-08:00","id":1546915,"title":"","content":"Rules from demon the fallen on unbelief are not a bad example to use.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}